'''war-tax''' (wâr′taks), ''n.'' A tax imposed for the purpose of providing funds for the prosecution of a war.

'''wart-cress''' (wârt′kres), ''n.'' See ''Senebiera.''

'''warte†.''' An old form of ''ware''<sup>4</sup>, preterit of ''wear''<sup>1</sup>.

'''warted''' (wâr′ted), ''a.'' [< ''wart''<sup>1</sup> + ''-ed''<sup>2</sup>.] '''1.''' In ''bot.'', having little knobs on the surface; verrucose: as, a ''warted'' capsule.—'''2.''' In ''zoöl.'', verrucose; warty; having a wart or warts; studded with warts.—{{smaller|'''Warted gourds,''' varieties of winter squash with a warted rind.—'''Warted grass,''' an Australian grass, ''Chloris ventricosa,'' with other species of its genus useful for grazing.}}

